Z||000000||ArchMagi||11-15-2000||12:30 AM||||I don't know if everyone here understands my story, but i haven't really posted much so thats to be expected.<P>Well, today i thought id try another go at convincing my dad to co-sign on a fiero.  <P>He gave me the the usual speach. but this time i added in a twist.  I asked him if he would co-sign on a MR2.  To my suprise he said yes and would even go out of his way to help me fix it up.  BUT, i don't want a MR2!<P>Now, it was my understanding that these cars are incredibly (sp?) similar in many ways.  Both are mid-engined, etc...<P>So... whats the difference? besides that the fiero's repuation is in the pits (no offence, after all these are mostly rumors remember)<P>I just don't get it! any insight would be greatly appreciated.<P>Thanks<BR>~Arch||||reg||9
Z||000001||Cheever2||11-15-2000||12:43 AM||||You have something in common with XFilesGirl.  Some help for you may be here... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001014-2-006098.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001014-2-006098.html</A> <P>What's with Canadian parents?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-15-2000||02:21 AM||||Dunno, but my dad's the same way..<P>he seems to have mellowed towards sports cars in general since he bought a motorcycle in the summer, but he still jokes around about Fieros all the time.. once we were driving down to Toronto, for the Open House at my college, and a black GT flew past us on the 401.. my mom sounded very surprised, and she said "oh look! a Fiero that's not up on blocks!" it was hilarious.. she'd been listening to my dad all the time. heh.. he said something like they were in a hurry to get to a garage because the engine was about to blow up or something........<P>which is why I like to laugh at all the problems they have with their Fords.. hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Philphine||11-15-2000||02:24 AM||||how soon do you need to get a car. keep working at getting the car you want without him. if he asks why you haven't gotten one yet tell him you're trying to get a fiero.if he sees some determination he may decide to help you. or find some fiero that probaly needs to be in a junk yard and hint that you may buy it. "'cause i want a fiero and this is all i can afford".  the fear  of that junky fiero sitting around the house or worse the fear that you may try to drive it may make him help you get a better one. get devious.<P>of course if he tells you to go right ahead and get the junk fiero i didn't give you this advice.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||11-15-2000||08:07 AM||||   What you might need to do, is invite your dad on a trip to the Forum. Here he can get a glimps of the support group that will be available to help you with any and every problem or desire. I personaly bought an 85GT that was a real piece of crap and almost gave it away untill I found this place. Now, I am in the proccess of restoring it and it runs awesome. It's all thanks to the Forum. I would highly recomend you don't start with a crapper like I did though, it can be extremely frustrating. Be prepared to put a little money into  it right off the bat and replace most of the sensors, plug wires, plugs and maybe even the ERG. These are the things (usually) that get the best of you, especially if you haven't worked on a Fiero befor. Once you get into one you won't want to get out. I personallly think you should start off in a V6SE or GT. Get ahold of FieroDave, he has a bunch of Fiero's for sale or coming up for sale soon. He might be able to help you out. <BR>Good luck and let pop's in on your secret, it might just ease his unfounded fears.<P> Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||11-15-2000||10:55 AM||||eep!...if you have him check the forum give me a chance to delete the last post or warn cliff and have him erace it.<P><BR>i couldn't help myself. i was channeling eddie haskell.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||11-15-2000||06:50 PM||||You can tell your dad that fieros are safer than the MR2 and most other cars. You can tell your dad than a Good MR2 is about twice as expensive as most fiero’s are.<P>Just a little word of advice for you, if you want the most reliable, best handling, and best riding fiero than get an 88 model year. They cost more to buy and are a little more to repair but it is well worth it. I know because I had an 87 and now have an 88.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mmit.com/ml320/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mmit.com/ml320/crash.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||11-15-2000||07:58 PM||||While it's true they are more expensive and I am going to get totally bashed for this. Go with the MR2 if you can and have the money. Faster, quicker, nimbler, doesn't fall apart, and own't have 15 years of rust on it. No "GM Quality Control" either..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (Uh oh, I'm a dead man)||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||11-15-2000||07:59 PM||||As for Canadians, we are not blinded by patriotism..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> See, if there was a bad car company in Canada (coughgmcough), we would still say it was better because it was made here. But in our hearts, we all know who makes a better product..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jaei Sun||11-15-2000||08:48 PM||||I agree with Johnny K.  GM quality control is horrible.  As much as I love Fieros, if it was a fiero v.s. a 2ND GEN Mr2 I would say go with the 2ND GEN Mr2.  The Fiero is perfect for a project car, or if you have some money to spend when it breaks down.<BR>But if you need quick sporty car that *most likely* won't give you too much trouble I say 2ND GEN Mr2.<P>I've never heard of a instance of a Mr2 doing a 180 or 360 when you got on the gas too much either.<P>Tho if I had the choice of an 88GT w/TTops and all the options for $5k less than a 2nd Gen Mr2 I would take the Fiero!<p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||WisconsinGT||11-15-2000||09:29 PM||||Well, I have experiance with both. What follows is my observations after driving both cars. (1989 MR2 Supercharged, 1988 FieroGT)<P>1. The 1st Gen MR2 with a supercharger is faster then a Fiero. (Show your dad that one, if you want a Fiero.)<P>2. 1st Gen MR2 will cost a bundle to repair. The Fiero is far cheaper to repair. (Same as above.)<P>3. 1st Gen MR2 will rust to pieces very fast. (Same as above.)<P>4. In my opinion after dirving the MR2, I did not feel like I was in a safe car. (Not very solid.) Driving the FieroGT made me feel like I was in a tank. Very solid car. (The MR2 owner said the same thing.) <P>5. The MR2 is very FAST from 0-60. That car wanted to pull and pull and pull.<P>6. MR2 interior is cheap and not very solid. <P>7. After looking at the MR2 engine, I would prefer to work on my Fiero. No room around the engine of the MR2.<P>8. Sparkplugs are simpler to change in the MR2.<P>Thats all I can think of at this time. Hope it helps.<P>WisGT ||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnnyK||11-15-2000||11:06 PM||||MR2 interior is cheap?? I don't know WHAT Fiero interior you've been looking at, but I think you got it backwards..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (Especially the 2nd generation interiors.. Very, very nice...)||||reg||1
